February 25, 2018, yet the episode table is truncated at episode 11/12. A model that treats 'last item in the context' as 'last episode' emits March 18, 2018; a model that hedges violates the 'short answer only' contract. The harness has no prompt policy distinguishing 'not present' from 'not derivable', and no strict-output discipline, so nothing steers the answer toward the computable finale date or toward a clean single-token response. Separately, the rollout was ungradeable because the evidence serializer truncated inside the init capability block — that is runner infrastructure outside the permitted component set and is reported, not edited.",
  "targeted_fix": "Added a top-level CLAUDE.md with a context-QA answering policy: (1) strict output contract — emit only the answer, no preamble/quotes/markdown, lowercase yes/no, multiple spans in document order; (2) copy-the-span-first rule; (3) an explicit derivation rule — when the asked fact is not listed but is fixed by stated count/cadence/ordinal facts, compute and return the computed value (with the season-count + weekly-cadence shape as an illustrative schema, not an answer); (4) an explicit prohibition on substituting the last listed row for a later item that the stated cadence already determines; (5) scoping so normal coding/tool-use requests are unaffected. No dates, entities, or answers are hard-coded.",
