answer-form guidance: hooks/hooks.json was empty, no CLAUDE.md existed, and the only instruction was 'Return only the short answer'. For a nationality question the model therefore emitted the linguistically natural demonym ('French') while the gold label is the country name ('France'), which exact-match scoring rejects even though the underlying multi-hop fact was correct. Because the scorer is outside the editable component set, the harness must steer the model toward the canonical entity form at the prompt layer.",
  "targeted_fix": "Added a general, non-task-specific answer-form convention: prefer the canonical proper-noun/base form of the answer entity over derived adjectives/demonyms/inflections (nationality -> country name), use names exactly as they appear in the context, and keep the final answer terse. It is delivered twice for reliability: as project prompt memory (CLAUDE.md) and as a UserPromptSubmit hook that injects the same short convention into every prompt via hooks/answer-form-context.md. No answers or task identifiers are hard-coded; the rule is a formatting convention that applies to any entity/nationality question.",
